    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T11:15:05Z",
    "body": "More follow-ups from PR #823's delta review (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/823#pullrequestreview-5857857241):\n- **`square_edges` false refusals.** A staggered plate with a clamp ear (30 mm) or 30 mm corner chamfers is refused as \"turned\". It's safe, but annoying. Suggested fix: accept when either the least or the greatest edge on each axis is straight.\n- **`LocateFixture`** on a plate carries its riders without clash-checking them (`locate.rs:138`).\n- **A plate's mesh changing without dropping its grid.** A same-name re-import, a script `cam.import` or `RepairModel` changes the mesh but keeps the stale grid; only `ImportFixture` drops it.\n- **Dropped mounts aren't shown to the user.** `drop_dangling`'s result is discarded (`project/apply.rs:822`), so a dropped mount only reaches the log, not the user's load notes.\n- **`MoveFixture::new`** joins warnings by hand instead of with `fixture_clash::join`, which also removes duplicates.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
